mode: "100644"
text: "# audience.md Template\n\nThe output of this skill. Every field must be something that **changes how content gets made** —\nif it wouldn't change a post, it doesn't belong. Keep it tight; the content skills read it\nconstantly.\n\nCopy everything below the line into `audience.md` and fill it in.\n\n---\n\n```markdown\n# Audience — {Business or Client Name}\n<!-- version: 1.0 · updated: {date} · derived from: brand-profile v{n} · evidence: {sources used / \"limited — assumptions flagged\"} -->\n\n## Primary segment: {label}\n> The one that moves the business most right now. Build for them first.\n\n## Segment 1 — {short label}  ⭐ primary\n- **Who (relevant traits only):** {role/identity that actually changes the content}\n- **Buyer vs follower:** {same person? or buyer = X, follower/champion = Y}\n- **Jobs-to-be-done:**\n  - Functional: {the practical progress}\n  - Emotional: {how they want to feel}\n  - Social: {how they want to be seen}\n- **Pains:** {what blocks the job / hurts now}\n- **Desires:** {the outcome they want}\n- **Beliefs:** {what they currently think — to meet or challenge}\n- **Objections:** {why they hesitate — content should answer these}\n- **Language bank (their words):**\n  - Problem: \"{verbatim}\", \"{verbatim}\"\n  - Desire: \"{verbatim}\"\n  - Objection: \"{verbatim}\"\n  - They call it: \"{their term}\" (not \"{our jargon}\")\n- **Where they are:** {platforms + mindset on each}\n- **Who/what they follow & engage with:** {accounts, creators, formats}\n- **Sophistication:** {beginner ↔ expert — sets vocabulary/depth}\n- **Transformation (before → after):** {the shift the brand enables}\n\n## Segment 2 — {label}  (optional)\n- {same fields}\n\n## Segment 3 — {label}  (optional)\n- {same fields}\n\n## Notes\n- {multi-audience notes, aspirational vs current, evidence gaps to validate}\n```\n\n---\n\n## How downstream skills read this\n\n- **`content-pillars`** turns the **jobs and pains** into ownable, audience-relevant pillars.\n- **`batch-content-plan`** uses **segments, pains, and objections** to assign goals and angles.\n- **`hook-writer` / `caption-writer`** pull hooks, pains, and CTAs from the **language bank** so\n  copy mirrors the audience's own words.\n- Treat the **language bank** and **jobs-to-be-done** as the highest-signal sections.\n\nIf a segment's fields are thin or marked \"(assumed)\", write conservatively and prioritize\nvalidating them with real evidence.\n"
